I reach my building.
I go inside.
My neighbour Asha is standing in the corridor.
Her dog Moti is with her.
Moti is very energetic.
He jumps happily.
Asha sees me and smiles.
"Hello Maya, how are you?" Asha asks.
"I am fine." I reply.
"The weather is very pleasant this evening," Asha says.
"Yes, there is a very nice cool breeze," I say.
Moti comes near me.
I stroke his head.
"What are you making for dinner tonight?" Asha asks.
"I am making dal and rice."
"And you?" I ask.
"I am making roti and sabzi," she says.
We chat for some time.
I feel very good in this city now.
I feel truly at home here.
